  "body": "### What is the issue with the Streams Standard?\n\nFrom https://github.com/w3c/webtransport/issues/797,\n\nWebTransport closes its writable stream as part of its cleanup steps, but [the corresponding algorithm](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#writablestream-close) directly calls [WritableStreamClose](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#writable-stream-close) without any check. And WritableStreamClose asserts that there's no queued close request. And thus if there was an existing [WritableStream.close()](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#ws-close) call from JS, this cleanup step triggers double close of the stream.\n\nShould the close algorithm check WritableStreamCloseQueuedOrInFlight and bail out early?",
